The favorable pricing initiatives for the year ended December 31, 2025 in all operating segments included both new and carryover pricing increases from the prior year. 
Fluctuations in foreign currency exchange rates, including the effects of our hedging activities, unfavorably impacted our consolidated net operating revenues by 2%. This unfavorable impact was primarily due to a stronger U.S. dollar compared to certain foreign currencies, including the Mexican peso, Argentine peso, Ethiopian Birr and Turkish lira, which had an unfavorable impact on our Latin America, Bottling Investments and EMEA operating segments. The unfavorable impact of a stronger U.S. dollar compared to the currencies listed above was partially offset by the
